    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0227" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg143"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beaupré to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-05-05"><hi rendition="#italic">May 5,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to advise you that
                    information has reached me through a private source to the effect that within a
                    week or two the Colombian Government will send Gen. Marcellano Vargas, a
                    sonin-law of Vice-President Marroquín, to Washington, to negotiate for better or
                    different terms in connection with the Panama Canal convention.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Beaupré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
